Usage: 1z build [options] <file.1z>

Compile a 1z file to a native executable.

Build options:
  -o <output>                   Output path (default: source with .1z stripped)
  --save-temps                  Keep intermediate C source and object files
  --compilation-stats           Print compilation statistics
  --compile-all-prelude         Compile every prelude word, not just reachable ones
  --allow-interpreter-fallback  Suppress quotation fallback warnings
  --interpreter-fallback=MODE   Interpreter fallback policy: true, false, auto (default: auto)
  --lock-interpreter-setting    Lock the fallback policy into the binary
  --link-static=LIB             Statically link library LIB (repeatable)
  --dump-aot-image-classification  Print AOT image word classification
  --dump-aot-image-c            Print the generated runtime-image C source
  --emit-runtime-image          Embed a runtime program image in the binary
  --target=TRIPLE               Cross-compilation target (e.g. riscv64-freestanding-none)

Global options:
  --max-memory=SIZE         Set memory limit (e.g. 128M, 1G; default 256M)
  --load-path=PATH          Add a module search path (repeatable)
  --stdlib-path=PATH        Override standard library path
  --prelude=PATH            Override prelude file path
